{
  "title": "Ziyarate Shohadaa-e-Karbala (a.s.)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "اَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا اَوْلِیآئَ اللّٰهِ وَاَحِبَّائَهٗ\nalssalamu `alaykum ya awliya'a allahi wa ahibba'ahu\nPeace be upon you, O intimate friends of Allah and His beloved ones,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا اَصْفِیَائَ اللّٰهِ اَوِدَّائَهٗ\nalssalamu `alaykum ya asfiya'a allahi awidda'ahu\npeace be upon you, O the elite of Allah, His loyal friends,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا اَنْصَارَ دِیْنِ اللّٰهِ\nalssalamu `alaykum ya ansara dini allahi\npeace be upon you, O helpers of the religion of Allah,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا اَنْصَارَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nalssalamu `alaykum ya ansara rasuli allahi\npeace be upon you, O helpers of the Messenger of Allah,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا اَنْصَارَ اَمِیْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِیْنَ\nalssalamu `alaykum ya ansara amiri almu'minina\npeace be upon you, O helpers of the Commander of the Faithful,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا اَنْصَارَ فَاطِمَۃَ سَیِّدَۃِ نِسَائِ الْعٰلَمِیْنَ\nalssalamu `alaykum ya ansara fatimata sayyidati nisa'i al`alamina\npeace be upon you, O helpers of Fatimah, mistress of the women of the worlds,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا اَنْصَارَ اَبِیْ مُحَمَّدِ نِ الْحَسَنِ ابْنِ عَلِیِّ نِ الزَّكِیِّ النَّاصِحِ\nalssalamu `alaykum ya ansara abi muhammadin alhasani bni `aliyyin alzzakiyyi alnnasihi\npeace be upon you, O helpers of Abu Muhammad al-Hasan, son of `Ali, the pure, the sincere advisor,\nاَلسَّلاَمُ عَلَیْكُمْ یَا اَنْصَارَ اَبِیْ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ\nalssalamu `alaykum ya ansara abi `abdi allahi\npeace be upon you, O helpers of Abu `Abdullah,\nبِاَبِیْ اَنْتُمْ وَاُمِّیْ طِبْتُمْ\nbi'abi antum wa ummi tibtum\nmay my father and mother be sacrificed for you – you were good,\nوَطَابَتِ الْاَرْضُ الَّتِیْ فِیْهَا دُفِنْتُمْ\nwa tabati al-ardu allati fiha dufintum\nand good is the earth in which you are buried,\nوَفُزْتُمْ فَوْزاً عَظِیْماً\nwa fuztum fawzan `azimam\nand you attained a great triumph.\nفَیَا لَیْتَنِیْ كُنْتُ مَعَكُمْ فَاَفُوْزَ مَعَكُمْ۔\nfaya laytani kuntu ma`akum fa'afuza ma`akum\nWould that I had been with you, so that I too would triumph with you!"
}
